<section image-layout="blank" id="3qEGBRvkCe" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="OsBjJOLiBY"><h2>Two objects reveal two kinds of disagreement</h2><p font-size="lg"><b>There was not one simple cause—and people wanted different political futures.</b></p><grid divider="3pt palette-3" image-aspect="landscape" image-shape="rounded"><grid-item id="wRLGkSjpK5" colspan="17"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/XQTLd20C7RL_p4c-gMTTi.png" saved-media-id="p3cnn68vgkswyyq" source="image.ai-generated" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Layered cut-paper museum illustration of a nineteenth-century tax paper beside plain coins and a red seal, with no legible text"><h3>Trade and taxes</h3><p font-size="18pt">Who pays? Who sets the trade rules?</p></grid-item><grid-item id="53M3K6Ds0O" colspan="17"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/3PnuHsD5EjGkp4xI6QlOm.png" saved-media-id="2rh0htpgbi8hp0l" source="image.ai-generated" image-style="southern-brazil-paper-museum" alt="Layered cut-paper museum illustration of a folded schematic regional map with no labels"><h3>Regional power</h3><p font-size="18pt">How much say should Rio Grande do Sul have?</p></grid-item><grid-item id="iAiDcYVlfk" colspan="26"><p role="eyebrow">Different political futures</p><h3>The argument pulled in two directions</h3><grid direction="vertical" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="9AS1N81jnj" background-color="accent" padding="14pt 18pt"><h4>Some rebels</h4><p font-size="18pt">Wanted a separate republic with its own government.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="6Cr2V9OkzX" background-color="palette-2" padding="14pt 18pt"><h4>Imperial government</h4><p font-size="18pt">Wanted Brazil to remain together.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid><p font-size="18pt"><b>Different people made different choices for different reasons.</b> No whole side was simply good or bad.</p><p role="caption">Source: <a href="https://cultura.rs.gov.br/upload/arquivos/carga20210405/27100547-anais-ahrs-v-16-1.pdf">Anais AHRS, vol. 16 (PDF), State Historical Archive of Rio Grande do Sul</a></p></grid-item></grid></section>